WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:08.149
So, rhenium is a fairly modern element, it
was only discovered in, I think, about 1925,

00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:16.450
so it is 80-odd years old. Your grandparents
could be older than rhenium, or at least the

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:23.390
discovery of rhenium. It is now becoming increasingly
important particularly in the manufacture

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:29.699
of aircraft engines. As you probably know
in aircraft engines you have these huge blades

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:36.030
that whiz round and round, and because engines
are going faster and faster at higher and

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:43.239
higher temperatures, they need to be stronger
and stronger. And rhenium is now an ingredient

00:00:43.239 --> 00:00:48.719
that can be put into the metal, making the
blades that make them behave more effectively

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:54.559
at high temperature and this is almost leading
to a world shortage of rhenium.

00:00:54.559 --> 00:01:00.410
So this is a sample of rhenium, ok. This is
a very, very nice metal, often used in catalysis

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:04.970
from the middle of the transition metal group
and here you see the very, very dark black

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:08.080
coloration of this very, very fine wire of
rhenium.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:17.740
The chemistry of rhenium is also very interesting
and, unlike technetium, rhenium is not a highly

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:23.360
radioactive material so that chemists can
easily study it, there are interesting reactions

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:29.750
of rhenium which will, under the influence
of light turn carbon dioxide, which is a very

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:35.049
inert waste material, can actually be activated
and be made to react to make something more

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:42.700
useful and also that there are other reactions
of rhenium, which I think will become more

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:43.850
important in the future.

